# Local Notes — tightbinding on this machine

TEMPLATE. On a new machine: `cp CLAUDE.local.md.example CLAUDE.local.md` and fill in.
`CLAUDE.local.md` is gitignored; this template is tracked.

Put here anything that is true of *this checkout on this machine*. Put facts about the
machine itself (which Python, which MPI launcher and its flags, shell quirks) in
`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` instead — that file is outside all repos and is loaded for every
project. Keep both kinds out of the tracked `CLAUDE.md`.

Last verified: <DATE>

## External documents

`CLAUDE.md` refers to these by filename only. Record where they live here, or record
that they are absent — "absent" is useful information and stops a stale path being
treated as real.

| Referred to in CLAUDE.md as | Location on this machine |
|---|---|
| `tmd_warping_note_corrected.pdf` | `<path, or NOT PRESENT>` |
| `revised_formula_sheet_eta.pdf`  | `<path, or NOT PRESENT>` |

